what REDS %789 named a class and fired again forty minutes later from a different hand: commit 00493b3be replaced INNER LOOP item 7 of construction/ITINERARY.md -- Prove on touch, the directive telling every lap to run the endurance runs -- with a duplicate Git nib line, exactly as commit 5f96df5e14 had done that morning. A rewrite aimed at a line is a deletion of whatever that line held, and every standing guard stayed green both times: nib_honesty reads the nib by its KEY and finds it whichever line carries it, ascii_document and tracked_link and the pin bound read bytes rather than meaning. The one tell is that the numbered list then reads 6, nib, 8 -- visible to a reader and to no instrument. %789 named the cure and left it unbuilt because the lantern had fired once. It has now fired twice, so build the loom: a scan reading every ordered list in every living pin and holding it to 1..N with no gaps, no repeats, and no foreign line between two items, refusing at zero, proven from both sides in a throwaway pen with the two real firings replayed from history as legs.
